# Constructor write probe

Whenever an agent must change a 1C entity (any draft, any document: status, field, new card, comment), construction itself:

1. Creates a test object marked `CONSTRUCTOR_PROBE`
2. Discovers the working write call
3. Stores the recipe in `local_run.write_recipe` / playbook
4. Deletes the test and sweeps leftovers

Do not invent write calls. Do not patch live business cards during formation. Published agents still confirm writes (`onec.erp_assignments_write`, `onec.odata_post`, `onec.odata_patch`) via HITL.

The probe tool is `onec.erp_write_probe`. Detection is `collect_write_intents` — any 1C create/update step, not one playbook and not only assignment status.
